    "created_at": "2025-02-28T16:18:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-28T16:18:34Z",
    "body": "Coming from Japanese Layout TF in W3C i18n.\nFor point [1], in Japanese we consider unicode-bidi as isolate is better, since 1) whole ruby will be lined similar to inline element but somehow special that it actually contains two or more lines (for rb and rt, or rtc) of inline text, 2) ruby container could have both of rtl and ltr text in parallel like rb with rtl and rt with ltr.\nNormal C and J text does not have word separator (or white space), and whole text could be continue as one continuous stream. Ruby block placed within one word along with characters could be rare in other scripts, but it is normal in C and J.\n\n/cc @kidayasuo",
